Lander(6l)        MISC. REFERENCE MANUAL PAGES         Lander(6l)NAME     lander - the arcade gameDESCRIPTION     _L_a_n_d_e_r is an implementation of the ancient ``lunar  lander''     arcade game.     The object of the game is to gently land a lunar  module  on     the lunar surface.  Landing with a vertical velocity greater     than 5 metres per second will generally result in fragmenta-     tion of the lander and loss of cabin pressure!     Scoring is based on which landing pad you choose,  how  much     fuel  you conserved during landing and the difficulty factor     of  landing  from  higher  entry  velocities  as  the   game     progresses.     Operating instructions are provided on the initial screen of     _l_a_n_d_e_r. A high score file is maintained.BUGS     None   known,   but   please    send    bug    reports    to     {utzoo,utcsri,lsuc}!hcr!stacey.AUTHOR     Stacey Campbell - HCR Corporation, Toronto, Canada, 1989.DISCLAIMER     Lander  is  copyright  1989  by  HCR  Corporation,  Toronto,     Ontario,  Canada.  Permission to use, copy, modify, and dis-     tribute this software and its documentation for any  purpose     and  without  fee is hereby granted, provided that the above     copyright notice appear in all copies.     HCR  Corporation  disclaims all  warranties with  regard  to     this software. Use at your own risk.